</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8bc3946-e6d3-11f1-8282-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000824-000950-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8bc3946-e6d3-11f1-8282-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000824-000950-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed7c7e6e-e6d3-11f1-9f2a-a97f735bc207</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:46:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31 climate talks in Turkey collapse</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-cop31-climate-talks-collapse</link><description>
EU member states on Sunday objected to adopting an 11th-hour deal that omitted explicit references to fossil fuels, the bloc's presidency said. The issue remains a major point of contention at the summit, which is taking place amid soaring energy prices and geopolitical tensions fuelled by the war in Iran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/758bc72a-e6d3-11f1-a018-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000618-000759-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/758bc72a-e6d3-11f1-a018-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000618-000759-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ac2101e-e6d3-11f1-b903-ffa836b73163</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:44:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Drone strikes hit homes, United Nations building in Sudan's capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-drone-strikes-hit-homes-united-nations-building-in-sudan-s-capital</link><description>
Drone strikes damaged residential homes and a United Nations building in Sudan's capital Khartoum early Sunday, with the army accusing neighbouring Ethiopia of launching the attacks. The strikes came as drone warfare intensifies in the country's conflict, now in its fourth year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bea80488-e6d2-11f1-82d9-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000406-000527-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bea80488-e6d2-11f1-82d9-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261123-000406-000527-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3ac1b72-e6d2-11f1-8307-49948e389e56</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:43:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian ship attacked near Benghazi in suspected drone attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261122-russian-ship-attacked-near-benghazi-in-suspected-drone-attack-ukraine</link><description>
Authorities in divided Libya's east said a Russian ship docked at the Benghazi port was hit on Sunday in a suspected drone attack, causing a blast but no casualties. There was no immediate claim of responsibility for the strike, but it comes as Ukrainian forces have stepped up their long-range barrages against Russia far beyond the front lines.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00042f96-e6c5-11f1-aeb3-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-230127-230255-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00042f96-e6c5-11f1-aeb3-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-230127-230255-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04bb6ea0-e6c5-11f1-b0dd-f5d5a174d315</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:37:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel’s Eisenkot slams ‘Jewish terrorism’ after attacks by settlers in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot on Sunday condemned arson attacks by settlers on Palestinian villages in the West Bank as “Jewish terrorism”. Israeli police said they opened an investigation into the attacks, which came nearly a month after an inconclusive election stripped incumbent Prime Minister ⁠Benjamin Netanyahu of his majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29c45bc8-e6b9-11f1-8d4a-479735d131b5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:29:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Democrat Hubbard wins North Carolina recount, clinching historic House majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority</link><description>
Democrat Chuck Hubbard was elected to the US House of Representatives from North Carolina on Sunday after defeating veteran Republican Virginia Foxx, who chairs the powerful House Rules Committee. His victory gave Democrats their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in the 2026 US midterms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e68dbef8-e6ae-11f1-838f-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26312701855096.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e68dbef8-e6ae-11f1-838f-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26312701855096.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41ea6d50-e6af-11f1-a80d-c7e3a0a7b0ef</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:16:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e68dbef8-e6ae-11f1-838f-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26312701855096.jpg">© Nathan Howard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Russian warship hit by Ukrainian drone at Benghazi naval base, Libyan officials say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-russian-warship-hit-by-suspected-ukrainian-drone-at-libya-s-benghazi-naval-base</link><description>
A Russian navy corvette docked at the Benghazi naval base ​in eastern Libya was hit on Sunday by a Ukrainian sea drone, according to local officials, hours before a cargo ship was also hit by a sea drone in a second attack. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky on Monday confirmed that his country's military was behind the strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/659e3cc8-e6a9-11f1-ae55-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326649718247.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/659e3cc8-e6a9-11f1-ae55-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326649718247.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59c27282-e6a1-11f1-8d36-99870da4d23e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:41:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/659e3cc8-e6a9-11f1-ae55-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326649718247.jpg">© AP via Vanto satellite image</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Burnham, 'Brejoin' & the Ghosts of Brexit]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit</link><description>
“The people of Britain have spoken, and the answer is: we are out.”
 
The words of David Dimbleby at 4.40am on 24 June 2016, as the Brexit referendum result became clear.
 
But nearly a decade on, is Britain changing its mind?
 
Prime Minister Andy Burnham has reopened talks with Brussels, exploring options for a closer relationship with the EU. But the move has drawn criticism from key figures behind Brexit, including Theresa May and Boris Johnson.
 
So what is driving this rethink, and where might it lead?
 
France 24's Gavin Lee speaks to John McTernan, veteran Labour strategist and former adviser to Tony Blair.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2bf9662-e6c3-11f1-97b6-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/d51701fa-2d32-46c1-9b89-ff9716ff196f.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2bf9662-e6c3-11f1-97b6-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/d51701fa-2d32-46c1-9b89-ff9716ff196f.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e32e232-e6ac-11f1-91aa-09eb8656efc7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:37:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Le Pen denies receiving leaked information from French interior ministry official</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261122-le-pen-denies-receiving-leaked-information-from-french-interior-ministry-official</link><description>
French far-right leader Marine Le Pen on Sunday said she did not receive, nor ask for, confidential information on an investigation into her party from a senior interior ministry official. She however could not say if other party members had benefited from the leaks. Hugues Moutouh, the civil servant under suspicion, has denied the allegations and asked to be relieved of his duties pending a probe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83540fda-e696-11f1-ba48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26324374289119.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83540fda-e696-11f1-ba48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26324374289119.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e7cb806-e698-11f1-998f-2b13d9c5e9d8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:47:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83540fda-e696-11f1-ba48-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26324374289119.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AP via pool photo </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Ligue 1: PSG extend winning run at Nice (3-2) but lose Désiré Doué to injury</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261122-ligue-1-psg-extend-winning-run-at-nice-3-2-but-lose-d%C3%A9sir%C3%A9-dou%C3%A9-to-injury</link><description>
A bittersweet victory for PSG at Nice on Saturday evening. The Parisians strengthened their grip on top spot in Ligue 1, but lost Désiré Doué for several months after the forward suffered a serious knee injury.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84817312-e613-11f1-8f47-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8969H7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84817312-e613-11f1-8f47-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8969H7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9151e4fe-e614-11f1-a16c-9b860d309282</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:55:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Drone strikes hit homes and UN building in Sudan's Khartoum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-drone-strikes-hit-homes-and-un-building-in-sudan-s-khartoum</link><description>
Drone strikes damaged residential homes and a United Nations building in Sudan's capital Khartoum early Sunday, with the army accusing neighbouring Ethiopia of launching the attacks. The strikes came as drone warfare intensifies in the country's conflict, now in its fourth year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c5eb51c-e693-11f1-9b46-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/5b43f69bec605872bb956153617567218ceba021.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c5eb51c-e693-11f1-9b46-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/5b43f69bec605872bb956153617567218ceba021.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d39bae0-e693-11f1-a9ff-1deb7bcd9931</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:38:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c5eb51c-e693-11f1-9b46-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/5b43f69bec605872bb956153617567218ceba021.jpg">© Ebrahim Hamid, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank attacks: Opposition leader Eisenkot decries "Jewish terrorism"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were set on fire in three villages in the occupied West Bank. Israeli soldiers were deployed to the area following the attacks, which local residents said were carried out by Israeli settlers. Gadi Eisenkot, a rival of outgoing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, condemned the acts on X, describing them as “Jewish terrorism”. Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">850a0628-e690-11f1-9770-d1608150d187</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:25:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian strike kills 2 in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strike-kills-2-in-kyiv</link><description>
A Russian attack struck an apartment building in the village of Dymer, just north of Kyiv, on Sunday, killing at least two people and wounding four others. The morning strike destroyed a five-storey building, while rescuers evacuated nine people, including a child. At least 11 others are believed to remain trapped under the rubble.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64f540a0-e690-11f1-92e8-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160646-160820-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64f540a0-e690-11f1-92e8-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160646-160820-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69d5042a-e690-11f1-b687-0df3944fcdfc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:23:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>The week in pictures: Xi hosts Trump and Putin, COP31 and new French protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261122-the-week-in-pictures-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-cop31-and-more-french-protests</link><description>
From the unprecedented Shenzhen summit in China that saw President Xi Jinping host his US and Russian counterparts, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin, to tough talks at COP31 in Antalya, Turkey and another week of French protests over the cost of living, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d97c630-e4c9-11f1-8b5e-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T080754Z-1839523102-RC2IROA511RL-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-COP31.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d97c630-e4c9-11f1-8b5e-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T080754Z-1839523102-RC2IROA511RL-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-COP31.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87ebbd6e-e677-11f1-a837-3fcfcd6ec6e9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:22:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d97c630-e4c9-11f1-8b5e-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T080754Z-1839523102-RC2IROA511RL-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-COP31.jpg">© Kaan Soyturk, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>"It can take years": Why the AI Riemann proof is far from settled</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261122-it-can-take-years-why-the-ai-riemann-proof-is-far-from-settled</link><description>
AI claimed another major scalp in maths on Friday, as Anthropic mathematician Levent Alpöge published what he says is a proof of the Riemann hypothesis, a Millennium Prize Problem, in 17 million lines of code that no human has read in full. Physicist Tony Padilla tells Tech 24 that verification could take years, and that Alpöge should share how he got there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbac99c6-e67c-11f1-91ce-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-TECH24-22-11-26-2027-ep-17-PAD.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbac99c6-e67c-11f1-91ce-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-TECH24-22-11-26-2027-ep-17-PAD.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da10684c-e67c-11f1-aaba-819df7ac864a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:18:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Peter O'BRIEN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel investigates West Bank fires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were vandalised and set on fire in four villages in the occupied West Bank, in attacks local activists say were carried out by Israeli settlers. Around eight vehicles were reportedly torched and racist slogans sprayed on walls, prompting Israeli soldiers and police to deploy to the area. The attacks come amid a surge in settler violence since the outbreak of the Gaza war in October 2023, with more than 1,100 Palestinians killed by Israeli soldiers or settlers in the West Bank since then, according to an AFP tally. They also follow recent sanctions announced by the UK and Australia against eight Israeli companies involved in settlement activity. France 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky shares further details from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdc5c032-e679-11f1-804f-f99043976363</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:47:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 COP31 ends without deal as EU rejects text for omitting mention of fossil fuels</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261121-latest-cop31-deal-sidesteps-fossil-fuels-amid-growing-divisions</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">6563dfb8-e66f-11f1-a862-bda202dca7d9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:22:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Indonesia factory hit by deadly blaze: Three killed and 36 missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-factory-hit-by-deadly-blaze-three-killed-and-36-missing</link><description>
At least three people have been killed and dozens are missing after a fire broke out at a factory in Indonesia producing sweets and snack products. Fifteen people were rescued alive from the plant, while firefighters were still battling flames in several parts of the facility more than 12 hours after the blaze began. The cause of the fire remains unknown, but survivors said it started in a cooling unit on the third floor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f94de65e-e66c-11f1-93f4-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-120836-121007-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f94de65e-e66c-11f1-93f4-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-120836-121007-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe92e70e-e66c-11f1-9cbd-af2c2c013b6d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:11:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Former Italian police chief found dead</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/former-italian-police-chief-found-dead</link><description>
Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni has expressed shock following the death of a former national police chief, whose body was found on Saturday. He had been under investigation over an alleged cover-up in an inquiry into a bombing linked to organised crime in Sicily. Jennie Shin reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9d7f9c0-e658-11f1-9bb1-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-101007-101157-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9d7f9c0-e658-11f1-9bb1-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-101007-101157-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af40808a-e658-11f1-b1a0-db25d08751fc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:25:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Princess of Wales opens up about cancer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/princess-of-wales-opens-up-about-cancer</link><description>
A new documentary titled Heal follows Britain’s Princess Catherine as she navigates life since her cancer diagnosis in 2024. The film tracks the 44-year-old as she attempts to climb the highest mountains in Scotland, England and Wales within 24 hours. In the trailer, she reflects on healing as a journey. Ophelie Jacobson reports.
